    "updated_at": "2026-11-12T17:17:10Z",
    "body": "PR #1213 updated after review (head `27dee0df`). The rule is now stricter. On a lathe or mill-turn setup, a post script without a `capabilities` line naming 1 or 2 posts only C-axis live-tool sections. Every other section is refused by name, with the manifest line to add. That covers milling sections, and also turning sections and on-centre drills, since only a turning post may post those and an unstated script is not known to be one. On a mill or with no machine it posts as before.\n\nCurrent pins (they replace the `post::dialect::tests::an_undeclared_mask_is_none_never_a_guess` named earlier, which was dropped when main's #1174 `work_voice` was adopted):\n- `camcraft-app` lib `lathe_voice::tests::an_undeclared_script_is_held_to_the_door_on_a_machine_with_a_work_spindle`\n- `crates/app/tests/lathe_workholding_mill_post.rs` `every_machine_dialect_and_section_cell_gives_its_verdict`\n\nMerges when reviewed.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
